dialogue cave_recruit_tank
title: A guard on the ice
trigger: ThemeStart cave
speaker commander $commander
speaker recruit $recruit
speaker backer $party:2

node meet recruit
  Halt. That's a Choir wagon on Anchor ice. Give me one reason my hammer stays on my back.
  -> reply

node reply commander
  The hammer is bigger than the one holding it, and it hasn't moved yet.
  * Because we stole it. -> stole
  * Because you'd lose. -> threat
  * Because we're not here for you. -> passing

node stole recruit
  Stole it. From the Choir. Out here people don't steal from the Choir, they kneel to it and pay.
  -> post

node threat recruit
  Ha. Plenty of things have told me that on this ice. The Watch's dead knights told me that. I'm still standing.
  -> post

node passing recruit
  Nobody passes the arches by accident. Either you're carrying the tithe or you're running from it.
  -> post

node post recruit
  My hold sent me to guard these arches. Every night they hum, and our tithe rides the beam up into the dark.
  -> beams

node beams commander
  The arches throw their light at the sky.
  * We ran from the tithe at Saltmoss. We're following the beams. -> follow
  * Guarding them for whom? -> whom

node follow recruit
  Following them where? The beams go up. There's nothing up there but the stone in the sky.
  -> doubt

node whom recruit
  For my hold. For the oath. The Captain stood in our hall and swore the tithe would buy us peace. I swore to guard it.
  -> doubt

node doubt recruit
  An oath is all a squire has. Why would I break mine for a stolen wagon and a story?
  -> backer

node backer backer
  It's no story. The Commander pulled the tithe out of the white wagon at Saltmoss, and the orb woke in their hand. Show them, Commander.
  -> orb

node orb recruit
  An orb, awake, this close to the arches. The hum just changed. Listen. It's answering you.
  -> ask

node ask commander
  The arch overhead hums lower, and the beam above it flickers.
  * Your tithe goes up that beam. I mean to find out where. -> truth
  * The Captain sold your oath before you swore it. -> oath
  * Stand with us, and you won't stand alone. -> offer

node truth recruit
  Mine and my sister's and everyone's in the hold. I've watched it go up every night and never once asked where.
  -> sister

node oath recruit
  Careful. That's my hold you're talking about. But I've heard the Captain laugh in our hall, and it wasn't a laugh for us.
  -> sister

node offer recruit
  Standing alone is the whole job out here. You'd be surprised how heavy a hammer gets when nobody's beside you.
  -> sister

node sister recruit
  Saltmoss paid the same tithe as my hold. If somebody's finally asking where it goes, I want to be there for the answer.
  -> joined

node joined recruit
  My shield is yours. I stand in front. It's what I'm for.
  do: JoinHero knight role=Tank
  * Then stand in front, Knight. We'll stand behind you. -> welcome
    do: AddTrust $recruit 10
  * Thank the one who spoke for us. -> credit
    do: AddTrust $recruit 5
    do: AddCohesion $recruit $party:2 10
  * Your oath was to the hold. Don't forget it was the Captain who took it. -> terms
    do: AddTrust $recruit -5
    do: AddCohesion $recruit $party:2 5

node welcome recruit
  Behind me is the safest place on this ice. Stay there and we'll get along fine.

node credit backer
  You were going to swing that hammer. I'd rather it swung for us.
  -> thanks

node thanks recruit
  Then it will. A hold knight remembers a debt like that. I'll keep you behind my shield.

node terms recruit
  I won't forget. I'll hold that oath against the Captain when we meet. Just don't ask me to like hearing it.
